the following gives the volume of the tank?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148019 1072 #uuid "085b9ec6-09cb-5083-beec-7fc3798cc33e" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148019 1073 true 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148020 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145844 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148020 1069 "q-62807" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148020 1071 "Lorraine has a birthday party. The rate $r(t)$ at which guests arrive to the party is given by the function\n$r(t) = 3\\sqrt{t + 1}$,\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in guests per minute, and $t > 0$ is the time in minutes.\n\nHow many guests arrived between $t = 0$ to $t = 3$ minutes?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148020 1072 #uuid "08983dc2-a7c5-546a-9359-a41f88833c50" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148020 1073 true 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148021 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145850 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148021 1069 "q-62809" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148021 1071 "The area, in square meters, of a horizontal cross-section of a water storage tank at height $h$ meters is modeled by the function\n\n$A(h) = \\frac{16}{3 + 0.25h^{2}}$.\n\nWater is pumped into the tank. When the height of the water is $2$ meters, the height is increasing at the rate of $0.5$ meters per hour. Find the rate at which the volume of water in the tank is changing with respect to the time when the height of the water is $2m$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148021 1072 #uuid "9df46443-fb95-522c-8a71-7720b6745ef8" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148021 1073 true 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148022 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145856 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148022 1069 "q-62814" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148022 1071 "The density of organic fossils in soil, in kilograms per cubic meter, at a depth of $h$ meters can be modeled by the function $F(h) = 5e^{-0.1h}$. How many kilograms of fossils are there in a vertical column of the soil that has a height of $10m$ and a constant cross-section of $2$ square meters?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148022 1072 #uuid "d6eb3bdd-3d0b-5924-ad4c-dca54b8d4a98" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148023 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145862 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148023 1069 "q-62817" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148023 1071 "The rate at which guests check into a particular hotel one evening is given by the function\n\n$r(t) = 3t^{2} + 2$,\n\nwhere $r(t)$ is measured in guests per hour and $t > 0$ is the time in hours since $6p.m$.\n\nGuests are also checking out of the hotel at a steady rate of $1$ guest per hour.\n\nIf there were $200$ guests in the hotel at $6p.m$, how many guests will there be in the hotel at $9p.m$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148023 1072 #uuid "22667ab0-d38d-572e-b2a8-f8517deb47de" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148023 1073 true 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148024 1068 #edb/ref 17592186145868 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148024 1069 "q-62818" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148024 1071 "The function\n$F(h) = {3 + \\frac{10}{h^{2}},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le h \\le 10 \\\\ 20e^{-0.1h},\\end{vmatrix}h > 10$.\ngives the number of kilograms of organic fossils per cubic meter of soil at a depth of $h$ meters. What integral gives the number of fossils in a vertical column of the soil that has a height of $20m$ and a constant cross-section of $5$ square meters?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148024 1072 #uuid "ca4c44be-b39f-5ef7-a8d8-b327d5638fad" 13194139533363 17592186