4139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148062 1071 "Gabrielle used an app to track the total time she spends per day on social media. For the first week of tracking, she calculated an interquartile range (IQR) of $2$ hours. The times she spent on social media per day during the second week (in hours) are given below:\n$2, 2.5, 3, 4, 4.5, 4.5, 5$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The IQR for the second week is $2.5$ hours.\n2. The IQR for both weeks is the same.\n3. There is a greater variation in the time she spent on social media in the second week compared to the first.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148062 1072 #uuid "4d6fc282-58b8-5f37-85a7-5342d7c8c465" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148062 1073 true 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148063 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146102 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148063 1069 "q-63335" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148063 1071 "What is the largest integer solution to $x < - 3$?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148063 1072 #uuid "040b012d-7264-5da9-adf2-9408c7aa4f46" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148064 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146108 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148064 1069 "q-63347" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148064 1071 "How many $\\frac{2}{3}$ cup servings are in $2$ cups of tea?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148064 1072 #uuid "5b7dd88a-1489-5155-b233-ffcea66256c6" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148065 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146114 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148065 1069 "q-63348" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148065 1071 "Pamela bought $\\frac{3}{5}lb$ of plums, and she wants to split them equally among $4$ of her grandchildren. How many pounds of plums will each child get?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148065 1072 #uuid "1f24e519-2260-5616-ba69-cfae219c60de" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148066 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146120 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148066 1069 "q-63349" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148066 1071 "Grace has $6$ gallons of milk. If it requires $\\frac{4}{7}$ of a gallon to make one whole pie, how many whole pies can Grace make in total using the amount of milk she has?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148066 1072 #uuid "09b75261-4fe8-5574-be71-e89bc7b4528d" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148067 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146126 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148067 1069 "q-63382" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148067 1071 "Jeremy spent all day in a field with a GPS navigator. He recorded his coordinates every time that he changed direction. The following ordered pairs were recorded:\n\n$(0, 0), (0, 3), (-2, 3), (-2,-2), (4,-2)$\n\nIf one unit corresponds to one kilometer, then what is the total distance that Jeremy traveled?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148067 1072 #uuid "918ed8c6-84a0-54cb-80e7-fd25a9e61bc3" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148068 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146132 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148068 1069 "q-63386" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148068 1071 "Mark is traveling on his sailboat through a lake. Every $30$ minutes he records his coordinates on a map using a GPS navigator. The data that he collects is shown in the table below. The coordinate system is set up so that the positive horizontal axis is aligned with the East and the positive vertical axis is aligned with the North.\n\n| Time | Coordinates |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $8:00$ am | $(-3, 0)$ |\n| $8:30$ am | $(-5, 2)$ |\n| $9:00$ am | $(-2, 2)$ |\n| $9:30$ am | $(-2, 4)$ |\n| $10:00$ am | $(3, 2)$ |\n| $10:30$ am | $(0,-1)$ |\n\nDuring what time period did he travel North?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148068 1072 #uuid "19de3044-9da5-5d68-9662-5f37db41ae21" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148069 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146138 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148069 1069 "q-63387" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148069 1071 "![](images/61/618ed2a95d27ed0fb713410678183491a3ee5adfe846fc62b6cde692fc5c964d.png)\n\nThe histogram above shows the distribution of daily incomes, in US dollars, of the workers in a construction company.\n\nThe frequency table below represents the same information. From left to right, what is missing from the table?\n\n| Daily Income ($) | Number of Workers |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $000-000$ | $0$ |\n| $131-150$ | $8$ |\n| $151-170$ | $5$ |\n| $171-190$ | $3$ |" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148069 1072 #uuid "22d33759-bcc3-502a-af9f-e1aa7c8bada6" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148070 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146144 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148070 1069 "q-63398" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148070 1071 "![](images/99/9970773cd1669641596363726cc0ab6378998ad75ce9d47d54ca34cb255b4260.png)\n\nThe histogram above shows the weight distribution of the vehicles loaded onto a ferry, measured to the nearest $0.1$ tons.\n\nThe frequency table below represents the same information. From left to right, what is missing from the table?\n\n| Weight (tons) | Number of Vehicles |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $2.0-3.9$ | $15$ |\n| $0.0 - 0.0$ | $0$ |\n| $6.0-7.9$ | $10$ |" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148070 1072 #uuid "7a918222-a7e9-530f-98b7-cbac078d1140" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146150 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148071 1069 "q-63400" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148071 1071 "The table below shows the coordinates of bus stops in a town. The coordinates are set up so that a difference of one unit corresponds to a distance of $1km$.\n\n| Stop Number | Location | Coordinates |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | Depo | $(4, 0)$ |\n| $2$ | Hospital | $(4,-2)$ |\n| $3$ | Theatre | $(2,-2)$ |\n| $4$ | Fire Station | $(2, 3)$ |\n| $5$ | Stadium | $(-3, 3)$ |\n| $6$ | Cinema | $(-3,-4)$ |\n| $7$ | Church | $(0,-4)$ |\n\nIf it takes precisely $5$ minutes for the bus to travel from one bus stop to another, then between which two bus stops is the bus going the fastest?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148071 1072 #uuid "37ad6bde-de63-56c6-9e90-ba1e5a79137a" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148072 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146156 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148072 1069 "q-63401" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148072 1071 "Samantha was walking in the forest with her friends. Every hour they recorded their coordinates on a map using a GPS navigator. Their results are given in the table below. The coordinates that she records are set up so that a difference of one unit corresponds to one kilometer.\n\n| Time | Coordinates |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ pm | $(-2, 0)$ |\n| $2$ pm | $(-2,-2)$ |\n| $3$ pm | $(3,-2)$ |\n| $4$ pm | $(3, 2)$ |\n| $5$ pm | $(0, 4)$ |\n\nAssuming that they traveled at a constant speed from $2$ pm to $3$ pm, what was their speed during this time interval?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148072 1072 #uuid "989cde88-67e6-5620-a25f-712c817a8ec0" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146162 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148073 1069 "q-63403" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148073 1071 "![](images/cf/cf50c9ca885aaab8b1209cefdc0f942a029775b29c219aa6762985dc99cddfd5.png)\n\nBrad, a baseball trainer, formed five groups of children according to their ages. The histogram above gives the corresponding distribution. How many of the children are at least $11$ years old?" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148073 1072 #uuid "e12371a2-f2bb-54b4-a0ba-74b4fa3d86d0" 13194139533363 17592186045585 true] [17592186148074 1068 #edb/ref 17592186146168 13194139533363 17592186